# The stress case: ~558 targets of macro-heavy, template-heavy C++.
#
# Measured: 14226 edits across 622 files apply with 0 conflicts, //absl/...
# rebuilds clean, and a second pass has nothing left to do.
#
# This scenario was blocked entirely on Clang 19, which aborted on
# absl/log/log_format_test.cc inside its own Sema (ExprClassification.cpp,
# `isLValue()`) while instantiating a local variable's initializer. Clang 21.1.8
# parses it. Getting from there to green then took two tool fixes that only
# abseil exposed: a return type spelled through a macro (`const ElfW(Phdr)*`),
# and the arrow being inserted in front of a trailing attribute
# (ABSL_ATTRIBUTE_LIFETIME_BOUND) -- the latter caught by `converge`, since gcc
# accepts that output and only the next parse rejects it.
REPO=abseil-cpp
RULESET=trailing_return_types
EXPECT=pass
